Vela: build mpv's library on macOS without Cocoa or Swift, from the SDK only.

1. Use the selected Apple SDK, never the runner's /usr/local libraries: mpv
   adds these linker paths even with cocoa/Swift disabled. Dependencies are
   resolved through the private pkg-config directory and the SDK instead.
2. Compile osdep/utils-mac.c for the Apple audio outputs when cocoa is off:
   ao_coreaudio_utils.c and ao_avfoundation.m call its cfstr_from_cstr, but
   meson.build compiles it only with cocoa (which needs Swift), so a library
   without cocoa failed to load (undefined _cfstr_from_cstr).
3. Build the VideoToolbox-to-OpenGL interop (videotoolbox-gl) on the
   plain-gl path, and link what it calls. video/out/hwdec/hwdec_mac_gl.c
   needs IOSurface, CoreVideo and CGL, and a CGL context current while mpv
   renders, which the application supplies through the render API;
   meson.build allows it only with gl-cocoa, which needs cocoa (and so
   Swift), whose frameworks were also what linked those three. Without it
   every frame VideoToolbox decodes is copied back to memory
   (videotoolbox-copy).

Only meson.build changes. Re-check all four hunks when bumping mpv.
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -882,2 +882,5 @@
                      'audio/out/ao_coreaudio_utils.c')
+    if not features['cocoa']
+        sources += files('osdep/utils-mac.c')
+    endif
 endif
@@ -1554,3 +1557,3 @@
 videotoolbox_gl = get_option('videotoolbox-gl').require(
-    features['gl-cocoa'] or features['ios-gl'],
+    features['gl-cocoa'] or features['ios-gl'] or (darwin and plain_gl.allowed()),
     error_message: 'gl-cocoa nor ios-gl could be found!',
@@ -1570,2 +1573,3 @@
     sources += files('video/out/hwdec/hwdec_mac_gl.c')
+    dependencies += dependency('appleframeworks', modules: ['OpenGL', 'CoreVideo', 'IOSurface'])
 endif
@@ -1599,3 +1603,3 @@
     add_languages('objc', native: false)
-    objc_link_flags = ['-isysroot', macos_sdk_path, '-L/usr/lib', '-L/usr/local/lib']
+    objc_link_flags = ['-isysroot', macos_sdk_path]
     add_project_link_arguments(objc_link_flags, language: ['c', 'objc'])
